# Discord features without Discord (ttl/discord.js + ttl/discord/*.js). Test bots never reach Discord, so this
# checks what the scripts compute: role keys (`ttl discordroles <p> expect …` prints "ttl: ..." on a mismatch),
# the Hall of Souls recap and the standings (bots are never counted: expect no TtlBot name in either), the
# read-only staff commands, and the ?bugreport refusals.
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] hall: recap preview" and no "[ttl] discord roles: TtlBot" lines.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotDiscU
ttlbot spawn TtlBotDiscD
@sleep 2
# A fresh Life 1: only the Life 1 role, no tier yet.
ttl discordroles TtlBotDiscU expect life1
ttl discordroles TtlBotDiscU dry
# Dark path: a few hours and eight villagers murdered → Survivor, plus Fallen once judged.
ttl karma TtlBotDiscD set play_time 216000
ttl karma TtlBotDiscD set mob_kills 60
ttl karma TtlBotDiscD set villagers 8
ttl karma TtlBotDiscD set advancements 10
ttl discordroles TtlBotDiscD expect life1
kill TtlBotDiscU
kill TtlBotDiscD
@sleep 1
# The Corridor still counts as Life 1; the verdict adds the tier role (and Fallen for the dark path).
ttl discordroles TtlBotDiscU expect life1 wanderer
ttl discordroles TtlBotDiscD expect life1 survivor fallen
# Recap and standings render (posting needs the bot: `ttl recap now` is a manual check).
ttl recap preview
ttl top
ttl staff status
ttl staff registry
# ?bugreport: RCON has no linked account, and test bots may not report.
bugreport test report from the rcon suite
execute as TtlBotDiscU run bugreport test report from a bot
ttlbot remove TtlBotDiscU
ttlbot remove TtlBotDiscD
